      "message": "When a specified `attr.label(allow_single_file\u003dTrue)` resolves to a target with zero outputs, `files_list` is empty and this returns Starlark `None`. But `None` is only correct for an absent optional label. A present target under `allow_single_file` *must* produce exactly one file, so resolving to zero outputs should IMHO raise the same `MustProduceSingleFile` error as multiple outputs.",
