      "writtenOn": "2026-07-13T05:01:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "When a plain `attr.label` or `attr.label_list` references a rule without setting `allow_files`, `schema.file_matcher()` is None, so this omits the `files` value and `resolve_label_or_file` also skips collecting the target outputs.\n\n`ctx.files.\u003cname\u003e` is defined for dependency-valued attributes regardless of whether direct file labels are allowed; `allow_files` controls validation, not availability of default outputs.\n\nI think this accidentally makes the common case of consuming a rule dependency\u0027s outputs through `ctx.files` impossible.",
