      "writtenOn": "2026-07-13T05:01:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "When `LabelKeyedStringDict` contains a label, `resolve_label_or_file` returns an `S::TargetRef`, and this immediately hashes it for the Starlark dictionary key. `TargetRef` does not require hashability, and the repository\u0027s existing `FakeTargetRef` uses the default non-hashable `StarlarkValue` behavior, so this advertised attribute kind cannot be converted with the existing session.\n\nI think target references need matching hash and equality semantics before they are used as dictionary keys.",
