      "writtenOn": "2026-07-13T05:01:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "When `allow_files` is an extension list and a rule target emits both a matching and nonmatching output, such as `.cc` and `.h`, this loop rejects the target on the nonmatching output; it also accepts a target with no outputs because the loop never runs.\n\nThe file-type constraint on a rule dependency is satisfied when at least one default output matches, while `ctx.files` still contains all default outputs. I think validation should probably check for the existence of a match rather than validate every output independently.",
